cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use VTOP Engine in research, please cite it as below."
title: "VTOP Engine: Verified Telemetry Object Protocol Engine"
abstract: >-
  A replay-safe, manifest-driven engine that moves telemetry from Kafka, files
  and syslog spools into S3-compatible object storage, and commits source
  progress only after the stored object has been verified.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Suliman
    given-names: Tamir
repository-code: "https://github.com/allamiro/vtop-engine"
url: "https://github.com/allamiro/vtop-engine"
license: MIT
version: "0.8.0"
date-released: "2026-11-12"
keywords:
  - telemetry
  - object storage
  - verification before commit
  - replay safety
  - Kafka
  - S3
